From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mbhangal23@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:14:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mob AI (Tier B, off by default): level of detail for idle
 mobs far from every player

paper-world config entities.behavior.ai-lod (enabled false by default). A mob
more than near-distance (box distance) from every non-spectator player, with no
target, not hurt, tamed, leashed, ridden, in love or raiding, runs its goal and
target selector update every goal-selector-rate / target-selector-rate ticks
instead of every 2, and villagers, piglins, hoglins and nautiluses tick their
brain every brain-rate ticks. Staggered by entity id. Running goals that need
an update every tick, navigation and controls still run every tick. Mobs near a
player are on the vanilla schedule on the very next tick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

